# Komodo — the keys stored in secrets.sops.json, one value each (`sopsgen
# apply` fills generated ones, `sopsedit` the rest). Values built from other
# secrets live in env.nix. Key set must match secrets.sops.json and
# tests/fixtures/stacks/komodo.sops.json.
# Rendered to /run/stack-env/komodo.env; Core reads it via env_file and
# compose interpolates the DATABASE values into postgres, ferretdb and periphery.
# Use HEX-ONLY values: they ride a postgres:// URL, so ':', '@', '/' or '#'
# would corrupt it.

# First admin
# Created on a FRESH database only. With KOMODO_LOCAL_AUTH=true (compose) this
# is the password login — there is no browser wizard. Single-token username.
# openssl rand -hex 24
KOMODO_INIT_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
KOMODO_INIT_ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme_hex24

# JWT
# Unset, Core generates a fresh one every boot and every restart logs everyone
# out. (Core<->Periphery auth is NOT here — it is the Noise keypair in the
# shared /config/keys volume plus KOMODO_FIRST_SERVER_NAME=Local.)
# openssl rand -hex 32
KOMODO_JWT_SECRET=changeme_hex32

# Webhook
# Verifies inbound git webhooks (Forgejo -> Core /listener). Must equal the
# secret configured on the Forgejo webhook. openssl rand -hex 32
KOMODO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=changeme_hex32

# Database
# Shared three ways: postgres initialises the `komodo` role with it, ferretdb
# connects to postgres with it, Core authenticates to ferretdb with it. The
# USERNAME is the fixed literal `komodo` in compose (backup-prepare.sh runs
# `pg_dumpall -U komodo`). initdb applies it on FIRST start only — to rotate:
#   docker exec -it komodo_db psql -U komodo \
#     -c "ALTER USER komodo PASSWORD '<new>';"
# openssl rand -hex 24
KOMODO_DATABASE_PASSWORD=changeme_hex24

# Git
# Core's read-only Forgejo credential: it clones the repo for the Resource Sync
# and every stack (Periphery gets it from Core per request). A PAT of the
# `komodo` bot user, scope read:repository, which is a read collaborator on
# idan/BasicBastardSelfhosted. Minted once Forgejo is up (pull class), so a
# placeholder until then — Komodo cannot read git before it exists anyway.
#   Forgejo (as komodo) -> Settings -> Applications -> Generate New Token
KOMODO_GIT_TOKEN=changeme_forgejo_komodo_read_token

# OIDC
# KOMODO_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET is NOT stored here: komodo/env.nix builds it from
# secrets/shared.sops.json, the one value Authentik registers the client with.
